# ERP Software — Development Environment Setup

## Project Overview

This project is an ERP platform intended for ISO/API-style audit and compliance management. The initial development environment is being built locally on Windows, with the eventual production environment planned on Google Cloud Platform (GCP).

## Development Stack

- Frontend: Next.js
- Backend: NestJS
- ORM: Prisma ORM 7.9.1
- Database: PostgreSQL 18.6
- Production Database: Google Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL (planned)
- Cloud Platform: Google Cloud Platform (planned)
- Analytics: BigQuery (planned for future analytics/reporting needs)

---

## Project Architecture

The ERP application is structured as a modular full-stack system with a frontend, backend API, and database layer.

### High-Level Flow

```text
Next.js Frontend
      |
      v
NestJS Backend API
      |
      v
Prisma ORM
      |
      v
PostgreSQL Database (localhost:5432 / erp)
```

### Responsibilities

- Frontend: user interface and dashboard experience built with Next.js
- Backend: business logic, API endpoints, authentication flows, and service orchestration built with NestJS
- ORM: Prisma handles schema management, query generation, and database access abstraction
- Database: PostgreSQL stores ERP data locally during development and will later move to Cloud SQL in production

### Local Development Architecture

For local development, the project is currently using:

- Next.js app in the `frontend` folder
- NestJS app in the `backend` folder
- Prisma configuration connected to PostgreSQL on `localhost:5432`
- Database name: `erp`

This architecture is intended to support a future multi-tenant ERP platform for audit, compliance, CAPA, and operational management workflows.

