## 12. Verify psql.exe

Run:

```powershell
Test-Path "C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\18\bin\psql.exe"
```

Expected:

```powershell
True
```

---

## 13. Verify PostgreSQL Version

Run:

```powershell
& "C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\18\bin\psql.exe" --version
```

Expected:

```powershell
psql (PostgreSQL) 18.6
```

The patch version may differ.

---

## 14. Add PostgreSQL to PowerShell PATH

For the current PowerShell session:

```powershell
$env:Path += ";C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\18\bin"
```

Verify:

```powershell
psql --version
```

Expected:

```powershell
psql (PostgreSQL) 18.6
```

---

## 15. Verify PostgreSQL Is Running

Run:

```powershell
pg_isready
```

Expected:

```powershell
:5432 - accepting connections
```

This confirms that PostgreSQL is accepting connections on port `5432`.

